---
title: "Electricity Fundamentals"
code: "ELE-157"
category: "electrical-technology"
credits: "6"
prerequisites: []
corequisites: []
---

Teaches the theories and laws of the flow of electricity, magnetism, inductance, capacitance, and the fundamentals of direct and alternating currents. Provides practical application by the use of test and measuring equipment, circuitry, and electrical apparatus. Lecture 3 hours. Laboratory 6 hours. Total 9 hours per week. Additional course fee applies.
